mium 12\n- The scrollbar in a drop-down box is not working properly\n- Example given: Language drop-down on google.com/chrome page\n- It was working fine in a previous release branch\n\nKey indicators:\n1. \"Drop-down box scrollbars broken\" - This is a UI/UX rendering issue\n2. The issue is about scrolling functionality in a dropdown being broken\n3. This is clearly a visual/functional defect related to how scrollbars are displayed or function in dropdown menus\n\nAccording to the classification criteria:\n- Class 0 (Non-Security Bug): Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems\n- Keywords like \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\" are indicators of non-security bugs\n\nThis is clearly a UI rendering/functional issue with scrollbars in drop-down boxes. There's no mention of:\n- Memory corruption\n- Buffer overflow\n- Information disclosure\n- DoS\n- Any security impact\n- Cross-context issues\n- Sandbox bypasses\n- Any exploitable vulnerability\n\nThis is purely a functional/UI bug where a scrollbar isn't working correctly in a dropdown. This falls squarely into Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 16168161159, "prompt_eval_count": 427, "eval_count": 493}}, {"id": "3480", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"c