em is specifically with embedding flash into a blog entry on WordPress\n\nThis is clearly a functional/display issue - an embedded video is not rendering properly. The bug is about:\n- Visual display/rendering problem\n- Missing content (blank space instead of video)\n- Feature not working as expected (embedding functionality)\n\nThere is no mention of:\n- Memory corruption\n- Buffer overflow\n- Information disclosure\n- Denial of Service\n- Security vulnerabilities\n- Exploitable conditions\n- Cross-context issues\n- Privilege bypasses\n\nThis is a straightforward UI/UX rendering issue where embedded content is not displaying properly. It falls squarely under \"functional defects\" and \"UI/UX rendering issues\" as described in Class 0.\n\nClassification: Class 0 - Non-Security Bug"}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 13410265865, "prompt_eval_count": 439, "eval_count": 493}}, {"id": "15929", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of Service (DoS). Distinctive patterns and keywords include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"h