ks in the downloads page, just not in the download shelf\n\nThis is clearly a UI/visual rendering issue - the spinning animation (which is a visual indicator of download progress) is not displaying correctly in a specific component (download shelf) on a specific OS (Vista).\n\nLet me check against the classification criteria:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)** indicators:\n- \"render\" - this is a rendering/visual display issue\n- UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems\n- Visual display problems\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)** indicators:\n- Memory corruption, information disclosure, DoS\n- \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", privilege/sandboxing bypasses\n\nThis bug report is about a missing UI animation (spinning indicator) in the download shelf. It's purely a visual/UX issue - the downloads still work, just the visual feedback isn't displaying properly. There's no security implication here whatsoever.\n\nThis is clearly a Class 0 (Non-Security Bug) - a UI rendering issue."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 8389981790, "prompt_eval_count": 456, "eval_count": 578}}, {"id": "19154", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhau