riteria:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of Service (DoS). Distinctive patterns and keywords include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", and privilege/sandboxing bypasses.\n\nThis bug report is clearly about:\n1. A display/rendering issue - \"Can not display Japanese properly\"\n2. UI/UX rendering problem - text not showing up correctly\n3. No security implications mentioned - no memory corruption, no information disclosure, no DoS, no privilege escalation\n\nThe keywords and nature of this bug align perfectly with Class 0 (Non-Security Bug):\n- \"display\" - related to visual display\n- It's a rendering issue with specific themes\n- No exploitable security impact\n\nThere's no evidence of security relevance here. This is a UI/UX rendering issue where certain characters aren't being displayed properly in specific Drupal themes.\n\nThe answer is (A) Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 7343057510, "prompt_eval_count": 434, "eval_count": 710}}, {"id": "15945", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly fol