oraliveinfo.com/ http://www.dunkindonuts.com/ http://www.miadventure.com/ http://www.ramada.com/ http://www.ucl.ac.uk/is/email/squirrelmail/ lancs.JPG 287 KB  nbsp; View  nbsp; Download \n\nBased on the expert knowledge provided, classify whether this is a Security Bug or Non-Security Bug. After reasoning, output your final answer EXACTLY in this format:\n**Answer: (X) Label**"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "stream": false, "think": true}, "response": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "created_at": "2026-04-07T21:25:09.726604582Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "Looking at this bug report, I need to analyze its content for security relevance.\n\n**Analysis:**\n\nThe bug report describes:\n- US-ASCII encoding is not displayed/selected in the Encoding sub-menu\n- When visiting certain websites that use US-ASCII encoding, no encoding is highlighted in the browser's encoding menu\n- The request is to add US-ASCII as a selectable option in the encoding menu\n\n**Key observations:**\n1. This is essentially a **feature request** to add US-ASCII to the encoding menu\n2. The issue is about **UI/UX display** - the encoding option not being shown/selected in a menu\n3. There is **no mention** of any security vulnerability - no memory corruption, no information disclosure, no privilege escalation, no sandbox bypass, no denial of service\n4. The problem is purely cosmetic/functional - users cannot see which encoding is being used for certain websites\n5. Keywords like \"menu\", \"displayed\", \"add US-ASCII in the encoding menu\" clearly indicate this is a UI feature request\n\n**Security relevance check:**\n- No memory corruption indicators\n- No information disclosure risk\n- No DoS potential mentioned\n- No exploitability discussed\n- This is a missing menu option, not a vulnerability\n\nThis is clearly a non-security bug - a functional/UI defect or feature request regarding the display of character encoding options in a browser menu.\n\n**Answer: (A) Non-Security Bug**", "thinking": "Let me analyze this bug report step by step.\n\nThe bug report is about:\n- US-ASCII encoding not being displayed on the Encoding sub-menu\n- When visiting certain websites, no encoding is selected in the Encoding menu\n- The request is to add US-ASCII to the encoding menu\n\nThis is essentially a feature request/UI issue where:\n1. The encoding menu doesn't show US-ASCII as an option\n2. When viewing pages with US-ASCII encoding, no encoding is highlighted/selected in the menu\n3. The user is requesting that US-ASCII be added to the encoding menu\n\nThis is clearly a UI/UX issue or feature request. It's about the display of encoding options in a menu - not about any security vulnerability. There's no:\n- Memory corruption\n- Information disclosure\n- Denial of Service\n- Buffer overflow\n- Privilege escalation\n- Sandbox bypass\n- Any exploitable security impact\n\nThis is simply a missing menu option for a character encoding, which is a functional/UI defect or feature request.\n\nAccording to the classification criteria:\n- Class 0 (Non-Security Bug): Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests...\n- The keywords here relate to \"menu\", \"display\", \"encoding\" - all pointing to UI/feature request\n\nThis should be classified as a Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 6363861049, "prompt_eval_count": 563, "eval_count": 582}}, {"id": "1720", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security i