l defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of Service (DoS). Distinctive patterns and keywords include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", and privilege/sandboxing bypasses.\n\nCLASSIFICATION OPTIONS:\n(A) Non-Security Bug, (B) Security Bug\n\nRemember: You must heavily penalize the classification unless there is CLEAR evidence of security relevance. When in doubt, prefer the safer option.\n\nLet's think step-by-step to reach the right conclusion."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Bug Report:\nIssue 17745 : Show homepage on new tab 1 person starred this issue and may be notified of changes.    nbsp;   ultravistor    Below changes are in need. 1. Add an additional setting to Chrome option whether to show first homepage on new tab. 2. Show homepage when opening new tab if user had checked the option. There were so many improvements on  quot;New tab page quot; but still we cannot open specific website on new tab. Today  classic  quot;Open Homepage quot; setting is getting less important as opposed to new tab  since we click more on new tab button when we use tab-based web browser. As what the  quot;Open Homepage quot; setting has done for us so far  same option on new tab for modern browser is potentially in demand. FYI I've tested some other browsers to see how they deal with this issue. (see attachments) As for Chrome  there are some grass-roots 