w on www.pconline.com.cn cannot be closed by clicking the \"X\" button\n- This is a UI/functionality issue where a window close button doesn't work\n- The expected behavior is that clicking \"X\" should close the constrained window\n\nLet me check against the classification criteria:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)** indicators:\n- Functional defects \u2713 (close button doesn't work)\n- UI/UX rendering issues \u2713 (window interaction problem)\n- General application behavior issues \u2713\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)** indicators:\n- Memory corruption - No\n- Information disclosure - No\n- Denial of Service (DoS) - No\n- Buffer overflow - No\n- Heap overwrite - No\n- Cross-context - No\n- javascript: - No\n- Redirect - No\n- Privilege/sandboxing bypass - No\n\nThis is clearly a UI/functional defect where a button doesn't perform its expected action. There's no indication of security implications - it's simply a broken close button on a constrained window. This doesn't compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability in a security sense.\n\nThe bug is about a window not being able to be closed when clicking the X button - this is a straightforward UI/functionality bug.\n\n**Answer: (A) Non-Security Bug**"}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 46279445209, "prompt_eval_count": 547, "eval_count": 522}}, {"id": "18439", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layo