bs are displayed incorrectly (too small) when performing rapid tab operations. This is a visual display/layout issue, not a security vulnerability.\n\nKey indicators:\n- \"tabs to show very small\" - visual display issue\n- \"Tabs appear very small\" - rendering/layout problem\n- No mention of memory corruption, information disclosure, DoS, or any security-related keywords\n- This is a functional/UI defect, not something that compromises confidentiality, integrity, or availability\n\nBased on the classification criteria:\n- Class 0 (Non-Security Bug): Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems\n- This fits perfectly under Class 0\n\nThis is a Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 32131312147, "prompt_eval_count": 507, "eval_count": 452}}, {"id": "19782", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of Service (DoS). Distinctive patterns and keywords include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\",