rs can't create application shortcuts at all\n\nLet me evaluate this against the classification criteria:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)** indicators:\n- This is a functional defect - a file (gears.dll) is not being copied to the correct directory during installation\n- The impact is that users can't create application shortcuts - this is a functional/UX issue\n- No mention of memory corruption, information disclosure, DoS, or other security vulnerabilities\n- No keywords like \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"memory leak\", \"cross-context\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", \"privilege bypass\", \"sandboxing bypass\"\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)** indicators:\n- None present in this report\n\nThis is clearly a functional/installation bug where a DLL file is not being copied during installation, resulting in a missing feature (application shortcuts). There's no security impact mentioned - no exploitation potential, no confidentiality/integrity/availability compromise in a security sense.\n\nThe inability to create application shortcuts is a usability/functional issue, not a security vulnerability.\n\nTherefore, this should be classified as a Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 11360164131, "prompt_eval_count": 391, "eval_count": 520}}, {"id": "1818", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \