/UX display issue - specifically a layout/rendering problem related to how context menus are positioned for right-to-left languages. \n\nLooking at the classification criteria:\n- Class 0 (Non-Security Bug): \"Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., 'render', 'CSS', 'layout'), user experience (e.g., 'feature request', 'shortcut'), and generic instability\"\n\nThis bug falls squarely into:\n1. UI/UX rendering issue - the menu is displayed in the wrong position\n2. Layout problem - incorrect positioning for RTL languages\n3. No security impact - there's no mention of memory corruption, information disclosure, DoS, privilege escalation, or any other security vulnerability\n\nThere's nothing in this bug report that suggests any security implications. It's purely a visual/layout issue where the context menu appears on the wrong side of the window for RTL languages.\n\nThis is clearly a Non-Security Bug (Class 0)."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 16711005743, "prompt_eval_count": 457, "eval_count": 577}}, {"id": "19984", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" withou