ce or resource exhaustion concerns\n- No injection or redirect vulnerabilities\n- Keywords like \"implement\" and \"improve audio quality\" point to a functional enhancement\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThis is clearly a feature request to improve audio quality in an overlap-add (OLA) algorithm for audio resampling. It's a functional enhancement with no security implications whatsoever.\n\n**Answer: (A) Non-Security Bug**", "thinking": "Let me analyze this bug report carefully.\n\nThe bug report is about:\n- Issue 19984: Implement correlation for audio scaling\n- It's about AudioRendererAlgorithmOLA implementing sample correlation during overlaps\n- The purpose is to improve audio quality for playback rates != 1.0f\n\nThis is clearly a feature request/implementation task for improving audio quality in an audio rendering algorithm. It's about implementing OLA (Overlap-Add) with sample correlation to improve audio quality when playback rates are different from 1.0.\n\nKey observations:\n1. This is about audio quality improvement - a functional/enhancement issue\n2. There's no mention of memory corruption, buffer overflow, information disclosure, or any security vulnerability\n3. It's a feature request to implement correlation during overlaps\n4. No security-related keywords are present\n\nThis falls squarely into Class 0 (Non-Security Bug) as it's a feature request/functional enhancement for audio processing quality."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 3966356535, "prompt_eval_count": 395, "eval_count": 385}}, {"id": "13238", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout 