's a failure of LayoutTests/fast/text/text-letter-spacing.html\n- This is a new test added in a WebKit patch\n- It's split off from bug 15873\n\nKey indicators:\n- \"Layout test\" - This relates to layout/rendering\n- \"text-letter-spacing\" - This is about text rendering, specifically letter spacing\n- This is clearly a visual/rendering issue related to how text is displayed\n\nAccording to the domain knowledge provided:\n- Class 0 (Non-Security Bug): \"Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., 'render', 'CSS', 'layout')\"\n\nThis bug report clearly falls under Class 0 because:\n1. It's a layout test failure\n2. It deals with text rendering (letter-spacing)\n3. There's no mention of any security-relevant keywords like \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", or privilege/sandboxing bypasses\n4. This is purely a visual/display issue\n\nThe classification should be (A) Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 5981360323, "prompt_eval_count": 387, "eval_count": 556}}, {"id": "18348", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature re