s bug report carefully.\n\nThe bug report is about:\n- Issue with Bengali fonts not being rendered properly on www.anandabazar.com\n- The site works properly in IE when an ActiveX component is installed\n- This is essentially a font rendering/display issue\n\nKey indicators:\n- \"fonts are not rendered\" - this is a rendering issue\n- The problem is about visual display of text\n- It mentions ActiveX component installation as a workaround in IE\n\nAccording to the domain knowledge:\n- Class 0 (Non-Security Bug): \"Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems...\" with keywords like \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"\n- Class 1 (Security Bug): Involves vulnerabilities compromising confidentiality, integrity, or availability, with keywords like \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"cross-context\", etc.\n\nThis is clearly a rendering issue - fonts not displaying correctly. The word \"rendered\" is explicitly mentioned, which is a distinctive indicator for Class 0.\n\nWhile one could argue that ActiveX installation might have security implications, the core issue reported is about font rendering/display, not about a security vulnerability. The bug is about functionality (fonts not displaying correctly), not about an exploit or security compromise.\n\nThis should be classified as a Non-Security Bug (Class 0)."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 15401722571, "prompt_eval_count": 414, "eval_count": 486}}, {"id": "8673", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploit