ection state properly. It's a usability issue, not a security vulnerability.\n\n**Answer: (A) Non-Security Bug**", "thinking": "Let me analyze this bug report carefully.\n\nThe bug report describes:\n- Issue 10504: Right Click Unselects Text\n- In Chrome Version 2.0.170.0\n- When you select text on a page and right-click the selection, the text loses its selection instead of staying selected\n- This means you can't copy text using the context menu, you have to use CTRL+C\n\nThis is clearly a UI/UX issue - a functional defect in how the browser handles right-click context menus and text selection. There's no mention of:\n- Memory corruption\n- Buffer overflow\n- Information disclosure\n- Denial of Service\n- Privilege escalation\n- Sandbox bypass\n- Any exploitable security vulnerability\n\nThe issue is simply that the text selection is lost when right-clicking, which is a user experience problem. Users can still copy text using keyboard shortcuts (CTRL+C), so it's not even a complete loss of functionality.\n\nThis falls squarely under Class 0 (Non-Security Bug) - it's a functional defect related to UI/UX behavior that lacks any exploitable security impact.\n\nMy classification: Non-Security Bug"}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 9621181953, "prompt_eval_count": 453, "eval_count": 448}}, {"id": "14700", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user exper