fect - the drag-to-change-route feature is not working properly. There's no mention of:\n- Memory corruption\n- Buffer overflow\n- Information disclosure\n- Denial of Service\n- Privilege escalation\n- Sandbox bypass\n- Cross-context issues\n- Any security-related keywords\n\nThis is a straightforward functional bug related to the user interface - a feature (dragging to change route) is not working as expected. This falls squarely under \"Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)\" which encompasses \"functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact.\"\n\nThe classification is clear: Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 28502502286, "prompt_eval_count": 432, "eval_count": 469}}, {"id": "13314", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of Service (DoS). Distinctive patterns and keywords include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", and