), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability.\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of Service (DoS). Distinctive patterns and keywords include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", and privilege/sandboxing bypasses.\n\nThis bug report is about:\n1. UI/UX wording - renaming a menu item\n2. Making the interface clearer for users\n3. Preventing user confusion about what \"Exit\" does\n\nThis is clearly a UI/UX issue - it's about making menu text clearer. While it mentions \"prevent horrible surprises,\" this is about user experience (not wanting to accidentally close all windows), not about a security vulnerability like information disclosure, memory corruption, or denial of service.\n\nThere's no indication of:\n- Memory corruption\n- Information disclosure\n- Denial of service\n- Privilege escalation\n- Any exploitable security impact\n\nThis is a feature request/UI improvement to make the wording clearer. It falls under Class 0 (Non-Security Bug).\n\n**Answer: (A) Non-Security Bug**"}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 13623489096, "prompt_eval_count": 413, "eval_count": 621}}, {"id": "18374", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to