ge\n- Steps: Go to a page, use Ctrl-F to find text, the find box indicates a result is found but nothing is highlighted on the page\n- When closing the Find box, the highlight then appears on the page\n\nThis is clearly a UI/rendering issue. The find functionality works (it finds the text), but the visual highlighting doesn't appear while the find box is open. The highlighting only appears after closing the find box.\n\nKey indicators:\n- This is about visual display/highlighting - a UI rendering issue\n- Keywords: \"highlight\", \"page\", \"find box\" - all related to user interface\n- No security implications mentioned or implied\n- No memory corruption, information disclosure, privilege escalation, or DoS\n- This is a functional defect in how the UI renders highlights\n\nAccording to the domain knowledge:\n- Class 0 (Non-Security Bug) includes \"UI/UX rendering issues\" and keywords like \"render\"\n- Class 1 (Security Bug) requires vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability\n\nThis is clearly a Non-Security Bug - it's a UI rendering issue where highlights don't appear properly."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 35638053549, "prompt_eval_count": 415, "eval_count": 551}}, {"id": "18875", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \