o exploitable vulnerability patterns are present.\n- This is purely a code maintenance/refactoring task.\n\n**Answer: (A) Non-Security Bug**", "thinking": "Let me analyze this bug report carefully.\n\nThe bug report states:\n- Issue 17415: mediaplayer cleanup\n- \"remove old stuff thats not useful anymore\"\n\nThis appears to be a cleanup/maintenance task for the mediaplayer component. The description mentions removing old code that is no longer useful. This is a typical code cleanup/refactoring task.\n\nKey indicators:\n- \"cleanup\" - suggests code maintenance/refactoring\n- \"remove old stuff thats not useful anymore\" - suggests removing deprecated or unused code\n\nThere's no mention of:\n- Memory corruption\n- Buffer overflow\n- Information disclosure\n- Denial of Service\n- Privilege escalation\n- Sandbox bypass\n- Any security-related vulnerability\n\nThis is clearly a housekeeping/cleanup task, which falls under functional defects or general maintenance - Class 0 (Non-Security Bug).\n\nThe classification should be (A) Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 50734580233, "prompt_eval_count": 366, "eval_count": 380}}, {"id": "5591", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 