 where it should\n- The cause is identified as the `float:left` attribute of a `<div>`\n- Severity is explicitly listed as \"Cosmetic problem\"\n- It's a layout/rendering issue\n- Works in other browsers (FF 3.0.11 and IE 6)\n- Only fails in Chrome 2.0.172.33\n\nKey indicators:\n1. \"Form not appearing where it should\" - this is a visual/layout issue\n2. \"float:left attribute\" - this is a CSS/layout property\n3. \"Severity: Cosmetic problem\" - explicitly marked as cosmetic\n4. It's about positioning of form elements on the page\n\nAccording to the classification guidelines:\n- Class 0 (Non-Security Bug) includes \"UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems\" with distinctive indicators including keywords related to \"visual display (e.g., 'render', 'CSS', 'layout')\"\n- Class 1 (Security Bug) involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability\n\nThis is clearly a CSS layout/positioning bug - a cosmetic issue with how elements are displayed on the page. There is no security impact here - no memory corruption, no information disclosure, no DoS, no privilege escalation, no cross-context issues.\n\nThis is a Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 8259187604, "prompt_eval_count": 556, "eval_count": 494}}, {"id": "13362", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"sho