haustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\"\n- Privilege/sandboxing bypasses\n\nThis bug report is clearly about:\n- Font rendering/display issue\n- Visual appearance problem (letter spacing too wide)\n- No security impact mentioned\n- No memory corruption, information disclosure, or availability concerns\n- Just a visual/UX problem where the wrong font is being used for Russian text on certain Chrome localizations\n\nThis is purely a visual display/UI issue with no security implications whatsoever. The text is still readable (just with wider spacing), and there's no mention of any security vulnerability.\n\nThis clearly falls under Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 16178575423, "prompt_eval_count": 538, "eval_count": 625}}, {"id": "17956", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of Service (DoS). Distinctive patterns and keywords include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", and privilege/sandboxing bypas