he SearchWiki functionality simply isn't present in the browser\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThis is clearly a non-security bug. It's a feature compatibility issue where a Google web feature doesn't work in Chromium. There's no security impact whatsoever \u2014 no confidentiality, integrity, or availability concerns are raised.\n\n**Answer: (A) Non-Security Bug**", "thinking": "Let me analyze this bug report carefully.\n\nThe bug report is about Google SearchWiki not supporting Chromium. The user is reporting that when they use Chromium to search on Google while signed in, they don't see the SearchWiki feature - just plain search results. They also tried changing the user agent string to Firefox's, but it still didn't work.\n\nLet me evaluate this against the classification criteria:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)** indicators:\n- This is a functional defect - a feature (SearchWiki) is not working in Chromium\n- It's about feature compatibility/support\n- No mention of memory corruption, information disclosure, or other security vulnerabilities\n- No mention of exploitable conditions\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)** indicators:\n- The user agent spoofing mentioned in the report is not a security vulnerability - it's a troubleshooting step the user tried to see if it was a user agent detection issue\n- There's no indication of cross-context issues, privilege bypasses, or other security concerns\n- No memory corruption, buffer overflow, or similar security issues\n\nThis is clearly a feature compatibility issue - SearchWiki doesn't work in Chromium. This is a functional defect, not a security vulnerability. The fact that the user tried to change the user agent string is just a debugging step, not a security concern.\n\nThis should be classified as Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 21489347251, "prompt_eval_count": 492, "eval_count": 537}}, {"id": "17606", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [