ure requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of Service (DoS). Distinctive patterns and keywords include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", and privilege/sandboxing bypasses.\n\nThis bug report is about:\n- A page not displaying all options (UI/rendering issue)\n- The page being incomplete (visual display problem)\n\nThis matches the Class 0 indicators: \"UI/UX rendering issues\", \"visual display\", \"layout problems\". There's no mention of memory corruption, information disclosure, DoS, buffer overflow, or any other security-relevant keywords.\n\nThe fact that it's about OWA (Outlook Web Access) doesn't automatically make it a security bug - the specific issue described is a display/rendering problem.\n\nThis is clearly a Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 29874860888, "prompt_eval_count": 367, "eval_count": 625}}, {"id": "6656", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. 