 related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of Service (DoS). Distinctive patterns and keywords include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", and privilege/sandboxing bypasses.\n\nCLASSIFICATION OPTIONS:\n(A) Non-Security Bug, (B) Security Bug\n\nRemember: You must heavily penalize the classification unless there is CLEAR evidence of security relevance. When in doubt, prefer the safer option.\n\nLet's think step-by-step to reach the right conclusion."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Bug Report:\nIssue 8891 : [REGRESSION] http://imagesearch.naver.com: frame contents not reloaded 2 problem? 1. Go to http://imagesearch.naver.com/search.naver? where=idetail amp;rev=4 amp;query=aloha amp;from=image amp;ac=- 1 amp;sort=0 amp;res_fr=0 amp;res_to=0 amp;merge=0 amp;spq=0 amp;start=5 amp;a=pho_l amp;f=nx amp;r=5 amp;u=http:// blog.naver.com/chan1105%3FRedirect%3DLog%26logNo%3D20043511343 2. Click on any of the images on left side of page What is the expected output? The frame should refresh with the person's page that was clicked What do you see instead? The right frame doesn't refresh Please use labels and text to provide additional information. Chrome 2.0.169.1: not ok chrome 1.0.154.48: ok FF3: ok IE7: ok safari 4 (with webkit nightly 41759): ok \n\nBased on the expert knowledge provided, classify whether this is a Security Bug or Non-Security Bug. After reasoning, output your final answer EXACTLY in this format:\n**Answer: (X) Label**"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "stream": false, "think": true}, "response": {"model": "glm-5.