s user experience but does not compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability\n\n**Classification reasoning:**\nThis clearly falls under Class 0 (Non-Security Bug) as it involves a \"UI/UX rendering issue\" and \"layout problem\" - both explicitly listed as indicators of non-security bugs in the domain knowledge. The misalignment of a tab title in an RTL context has zero security implications.\n\n**Answer: (A) Non-Security Bug**", "thinking": "Let me analyze this bug report carefully.\n\nThe bug report is about:\n- RTL (Right-to-Left) Gears dialog\n- Tab title is left aligned when it should be right aligned\n- This is a UI/layout issue in a Hebrew RTL context\n- The Gears dialog itself is in RTL layout which is correct, but the tab title alignment is wrong\n\nThis is clearly a UI/UX rendering issue related to:\n- Layout/alignment problems\n- Visual display issue\n- Right-to-left text alignment\n\nBased on the domain knowledge provided:\n- Class 0 (Non-Security Bug) includes \"UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems\"\n- Keywords like \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\" are indicators of Class 0\n\nThis bug has no security implications:\n- No memory corruption\n- No information disclosure\n- No denial of service\n- No privilege escalation\n- No exploitable security impact\n\nThis is purely a visual/layout alignment issue where the tab title should be right-aligned for RTL (Right-to-Left) languages but is currently left-aligned.\n\nThis falls squarely into Class 0 (Non-Security Bug).\n\nMy answer is (A) Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 6422023576, "prompt_eval_count": 504, "eval_count": 503}}, {"id": "3969", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when ma