ass 0 (Non-Security Bug): Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display, user experience, and generic instability.\n- Class 1 (Security Bug): Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or DoS. Distinctive patterns include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", and privilege/sandboxing bypasses.\n\nThis bug report has:\n- No memory corruption indicators\n- No information disclosure\n- No DoS implications\n- No security-related keywords\n- It's purely about the inability to interact with a form field (UI/UX issue)\n\nThis is clearly a Non-Security Bug - it's a UI interaction problem where a user can't click into a text field."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 19570398463, "prompt_eval_count": 398, "eval_count": 571}}, {"id": "3347", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compro