\n- Issue 16741: Unable to scroll on certain pages containing frames\n- The user cannot scroll with keyboard, mousewheel, or dragging the scrollbar\n- The issue involves frames (iframes)\n- It's a UI/interaction issue where scrolling doesn't work properly\n- The user needs to click or press tab to change focus to make scrolling work again\n\nLet me check against the classification criteria:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)** indicators:\n- This is a functional defect - scrolling doesn't work as expected\n- It's related to user experience/interaction (scrolling, focus issues)\n- No mention of memory corruption, buffer overflow, information disclosure, or DoS\n- No security-related keywords like \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", or privilege/sandboxing bypasses\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)** indicators:\n- None apparent in this report\n\nThe bug is about scrolling functionality being broken on pages with frames. This is a UI/UX issue - the user can't scroll properly and needs to click around or press tab to regain scrolling ability. There's no indication of security implications like memory corruption, information disclosure, or denial of service in the security sense.\n\nWhile frames/iframes can sometimes have security implications (like cross-frame scripting), this particular bug report is specifically about the inability to scroll - a pure usability/functionality issue.\n\nTherefore, this is a Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 12148115079, "prompt_eval_count": 662, "eval_count": 585}}, {"id": "17841", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your