 "Let me analyze this bug report carefully.\n\nThe bug report is about:\n- Issue 6676: [REQUESTED FEATURE] Auto pause downloads on program quit\n- The user is requesting a feature where downloads automatically pause when you quit the program\n- The user accidentally quit Chrome and had to restart a download from the beginning\n\nKey observations:\n1. This is explicitly marked as a \"[REQUESTED FEATURE]\" - it's a feature request\n2. The issue is about convenience/user experience - wanting downloads to pause instead of cancel when quitting\n3. There's no security vulnerability mentioned\n4. No memory corruption, information disclosure, privilege escalation, or denial of service\n5. No exploitable security impact\n\nAccording to the classification criteria:\n- Class 0 (Non-Security Bug): Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to \"feature request\"\n- Class 1 (Security Bug): Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability\n\nThis is clearly a feature request about improving user experience with downloads. It has no security implications - it's about convenience (not having to restart downloads) rather than any security vulnerability.\n\nThis should be classified as Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 4953617531, "prompt_eval_count": 409, "eval_count": 532}}, {"id": "9514", "ground_truth": "1", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, fea