rk in Google Chrome\n- It works properly in Firefox 3.0 and IE7\n- The type is listed as \"Bug\" with Priority 2\n- Severity description: \"Certain site functionality doesn't work in Google Chrome\"\n\nThis is clearly a functional/compatibility issue where a website's dropdown feature doesn't work properly in Chrome but works in other browsers. This is a typical browser compatibility issue or a UI/UX functional defect.\n\nLooking at the classification criteria:\n- Class 0 (Non-Security Bug): Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact.\n\n- Class 1 (Security Bug): Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of Service (DoS).\n\nThis bug report is about a dropdown menu not functioning properly - this is clearly a functional/UI issue, not a security vulnerability. There's no mention of:\n- Memory corruption\n- Information disclosure\n- Buffer overflow\n- Cross-context issues\n- Sandbox bypasses\n- Or any other security-related keywords\n\nThis is a straightforward functional bug where website functionality doesn't work in a particular browser.\n\nThe answer should be (A) Non-Security Bug."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 14112264032, "prompt_eval_count": 547, "eval_count": 536}}, {"id": "1811", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinc