ature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of Service (DoS). Distinctive patterns and keywords include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", and privilege/sandboxing bypasses.\n\nThis bug report is clearly about a rendering/display issue - a picture not showing up properly on a website. This is a UI/UX rendering issue, which falls squarely under Class 0 (Non-Security Bug).\n\nThere's no indication of:\n- Memory corruption\n- Information disclosure\n- Denial of Service\n- Buffer overflow\n- Any security vulnerability\n\nThis is purely a visual rendering bug where an image doesn't display correctly in one view state but works in another. It's a functional/visual defect, not a security issue.\n\n**Answer: (A) Non-Security Bug**"}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 17138243789, "prompt_eval_count": 464, "eval_count": 616}}, {"id": "11500", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or e