keywords include \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", and privilege/sandboxing bypasses.\n\nCLASSIFICATION OPTIONS:\n(A) Non-Security Bug, (B) Security Bug\n\nRemember: You must heavily penalize the classification unless there is CLEAR evidence of security relevance. When in doubt, prefer the safer option.\n\nLet's think step-by-step to reach the right conclusion."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Bug Report:\nIssue 16127 : Merge generated c files (from webcore idls) to a single compile unit 1 person starred this issue and may be notified of changes.    nbsp;   maruelatchromium    We currently have link failures because webcore.lib is too large in official WPO builds. We need to reduce the size of webcore.lib  in the short term  the easiest way is to simply split it in two. Also waiting on Microsoft for a fix but will probably require switching to VS2008 which adds its own issues. \n\nBased on the expert knowledge provided, classify whether this is a Security Bug or Non-Security Bug. After reasoning, output your final answer EXACTLY in this format:\n**Answer: (X) Label**"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "stream": false, "think": true}, "response": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "created_at": "2026-04-07T22:23:12.768722497Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "Looking at this bug report, I need to analyze whether it describes a security vulnerability or a non-security issue.\n\n**Analysis:**\n\nThe report describes:\n- Link failures because `webcore.lib` is too large in official WPO (Whole Program Optimization) builds\n- A need to reduce the size of `webcore.lib`\n- A short-term workaround of splitting the library in two\n- Waiting for a Microsoft fix or potentially switching to VS2008\n\n**Key observations:**\n1. This is a **build/compilation infrastructure issue** - the library is exceeding size limits that cause the linker to fail\n2. There is **no mention of memory corruption, information disclosure, privilege escalation, or any exploitable condition**\n3. The \"failure\" here is a build tool limitation, not a runtime vulnerability that an attacker could exploit\n4. The proposed solutions (merging compile units, splitting the library, switching compilers) are all standard build system workarounds\n5. No security-related keywords or patterns are present (no \"overflow\", \"exhaustion\", \"bypass\", \"disclosure\", etc.)\n\nThis is a straightforward build engineering problem - the library size exceeds linker capacity for certain build configurations. It lacks any security impact on confidentiality, integrity, or availability of the running application.\n\n**Answer: (A) Non-Security Bug**", "thinking": "Let me analyze this bug report carefully.\n\nThe issue is about:\n- Merge generated c files (from webcore idls) to a single compile unit\n- Link failures because webcore.lib is too large in official WPO builds\n- Need to reduce the size of webcore.lib\n- Short term fix is to split it in two\n- Waiting on Microsoft for a fix or switching to VS2008\n\nThis is clearly a build/compilation issue related to:\n1. Library size being too large for the linker\n2. Whole Program Optimization (WPO) builds failing\n3. A workaround involving splitting the library or merging compile units\n\nThis is a build infrastructure/compilation problem, not a security vulnerability. There's no mention of:\n- Memory corruption\n- Information disclosure\n- Denial of Service vulnerabilities\n- Buffer overflows\n- Privilege escalation\n- Any exploitable security impact\n\nThis is purely a build system limitation issue where the library is too large and causes link failures. It's a functional/infrastructure problem, not a security bug.\n\nClassification: Non-Security Bug (Class 0)"}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 5332591632, "prompt_eval_count": 435, "eval_count": 504}}, {"id": "13866", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "gl