erfectly with Class 0 indicators such as \"render\", \"CSS\", and \"layout\" problems. There is absolutely no evidence of any security vulnerability - no confidentiality, integrity, or availability compromise.\n\n**Answer: (A) Non-Security Bug**", "thinking": "Let me analyze this bug report carefully.\n\nThe bug report describes:\n1. iGoogle displays all windows/widgets (e-mail, weather, news, etc.) in one giant column on the left\n2. It doesn't allow the user to separate them into different sections (middle and right side)\n3. This is essentially a layout/display issue\n\nLet me check against the classification criteria:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)** indicators:\n- \"layout problems\" - YES, this is clearly a layout issue\n- \"UI/UX rendering issues\" - YES, this is about how content is displayed/rendered\n- Keywords like \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\" - This fits the pattern of a layout/display problem\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)** indicators:\n- Memory corruption, information disclosure, DoS - NO\n- \"memory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", privilege/sandboxing bypasses - NONE present\n\nThis is clearly a UI/layout rendering issue where the iGoogle page is not properly displaying its widgets in multiple columns. There's no security implication mentioned or implied - no data exposure, no memory corruption, no privilege escalation, no denial of service. It's simply a display/layout problem.\n\nThis clearly falls under Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 22404120429, "prompt_eval_count": 501, "eval_count": 526}}, {"id": "17669", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this