emory leak\", \"buffer overflow\", \"heap overwrite\", \"cross-context\", \"exhaustion\", \"javascript:\", \"redirect\", \"advisory\", privilege/sandboxing bypasses\n- None of these are present in this report\n\nThe bug is about a failing layout test where a scrollbar is missing in an iframe. This is clearly a visual/rendering issue - the scrollbar isn't displaying correctly. This falls squarely into the Non-Security Bug category as it's a UI rendering issue.\n\nThere's no indication of:\n- Memory corruption\n- Information disclosure\n- Denial of service\n- Privilege escalation\n- Any exploitable security impact\n\nThe fact that it involves an iframe doesn't automatically make it a security issue - this is specifically about the scrollbar rendering, not about cross-origin or cross-context security issues.\n\nThis is clearly a Class 0 (Non-Security Bug) - a layout/rendering issue."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 45409830909, "prompt_eval_count": 424, "eval_count": 666}}, {"id": "16913", "ground_truth": "0", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in bug report classification for security vulnerability detection.\n\nTo ensure extreme accuracy, you MUST strictly follow this domain knowledge when making your decision:\n\n**Class 0 (Non-Security Bug)**: Encompasses functional defects, UI/UX rendering issues, layout problems, feature requests, and general application crashes that lack exploitable security impact. Distinctive indicators include keywords related to visual display (e.g., \"render\", \"CSS\", \"layout\"), user experience (e.g., \"feature request\", \"shortcut\"), and generic instability (e.g., \"crash\" without memory corruption or exhaustion context).\n\n**Class 1 (Security Bug)**: Involves vulnerabilities that compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, such as memory corruption, information disclosure, or Denial of